# 032 - there is no truthiness (§6/.40), so ! is Bool-only and !1 is a Type
# error rather than false. Both engines route it through the one Bool gate,
# Value::as_bool, whose landed message is `expected Bool, got <T>` - which is
# why this message names no operator.
--- source
print !1;
--- expect
error: Type at line 1: expected Bool, got Int
